{"name":"Reindeer Moss","hex":"#bdf8a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"reindeer moss","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lichen (Cladonia rangiferina) that grows in areas of alpine tundra."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reindeer_moss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cladonia rangiferina","blocks":[{"text":"Cladonia rangiferina, also known as reindeer cup lichen, reindeer lichen or grey reindeer lichen, is a light-coloured fruticose, cup lichen species in the family Cladoniaceae. It grows in both hot and cold climates in well-drained, open environments. Found primarily in areas of alpine tundra, it is extremely cold-hardy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Cladonia_rangiferina_205412.jpg/330px-Cladonia_rangiferina_205412.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cladonia_rangiferina","wikidata":"Q248744"},{"title":"Reindeer","blocks":[{"text":"The reindeer or caribou is a species of deer with circumpolar distribution, native to the Arctic, subarctic, tundra, boreal, and mountainous regions of Northern Europe, Siberia, and North America. It is the only representative of the genus Rangifer. More recent studies suggest the splitting of reindeer and caribou. \"All caribou and reindeer throughout the world are considered to be the same species, but there are 7 subspecies.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Reinbukken_p%C3%A5_frisk_gr%C3%B8nt_beite._-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Reinbukken_p%C3%A5_frisk_gr%C3%B8nt_beite._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reindeer","wikidata":"Q39624"},{"title":"Moss","blocks":[{"text":"Mosses are small, non-vascular flowerless plants in the taxonomic division Bryophyta sensu stricto. Bryophyta sensu lato may also refer to the parent group, bryophytes, which comprises liverworts, mosses, and hornworts. Mosses typically form dense green clumps or mats, often in damp or shady locations. The individual plants are usually composed of simple leaves that are generally only one cell thick, attached to a stem that may be branched or unbranched and has only a limited role in conducting water and nutrients. Although some species have conducting tissues, these are generally poorly developed and structurally different from similar tissue found in vascular plants. Mosses do not have seeds and after fertilisation develop sporophytes with unbranched stalks topped with single capsules containing spores. They are typically 0.2–10 cm (0.1–3.9 in) tall, though some species are much larger. Dawsonia superba, the tallest moss in the world, can grow to 60 cm (24 in) in height. There are approximately 12,000 species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg/330px-Tionesta-ac-moss2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss","wikidata":"Q25347"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG/500px-Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG/1280px-Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG/500px-Cladonia_portentosa_top.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Top view of C. rangiferina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACladonia_portentosa_top.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG/500px-Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG/1280px-Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG/500px-Cladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The underside of C. rangiferina","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACladonia_rangifera_underside.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg/500px-Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg/1280px-Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg/500px-Braund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brown dune on Spiekeroog, Germany, showing Cladonia rangiferina growing beside black crowberry (Empetrum nigrum).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABraund%C3%BCnenlandschaft_auf_Spiekeroog_08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Barren_ground_caribou_grazing_with_autumn_foliage_in_background.jpg/500px-Barren_ground_caribou_grazing_with_autumn_foliage_in_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Barren_ground_caribou_grazing_with_autumn_foliage_in_background.jpg/1280px-Barren_ground_caribou_grazing_with_autumn_foliage_in_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa